# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/capital_port.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event docks_day_labour
# en: Hands Wanted
title [82086c] = 招工
# en: {&A foreman on the wharf is shouting for hands: a ship from somewhere hot is in with a hold of oranges, and the tide won't wait. Day rates, cash at the gangplank. The dockers look at your academy scarf and grin.|"Hands wanted," shouts a foreman on the wharf. "Barrels! Mind your toes!" He sees your scarf. "A wizard. Can you lift, wizard?"|A wool ship from the north is in, the crane on her berth has stuck, and her foreman jerks a thumb at the hold for anybody standing still. You're standing still.}
text [0ab34f] = {&码头上一个工头在吆喝招人：一条从炎热地方来的船满舱橘子进了港，潮水可不等人。按天算钱，跳板边现结。码头工人们看看你的学院围巾，咧嘴笑了。|“招人手！”码头上一个工头喊，“搬桶！当心脚趾！”他看见了你的围巾。“巫师啊。搬得动吗，巫师？”|一条北方来的羊毛船进了港，泊位上的吊车卡住了，船上的工头冲任何站着不动的人朝货舱一摆大拇指。你正站着不动。}
# en: A busy harbour wharf, cranes and barrels, a foreman with a slate shouting for day labourers, a line of dockers, a student rolling up their sleeves.
scene [9b763a] = 繁忙的港口码头，吊车和木桶，一个拿着石板的工头吆喝着招短工，一排码头工人，一个学生正在卷袖子。
# en: Work the hold
opt.left.label [d23dcc] = 下舱干活
# en: {&You carry oranges up the gangplank until your arms forget being arms. At the end the foreman pays you in coin and three oranges. The dockers have stopped grinning and started calling you by name.|Barrels all afternoon. You float one with a spell when no one's looking, and the foreman sees, and says nothing, and pays you a little extra. Your back aches anyway.|You unstick the crane with a word and a shove, and the whole wharf cheers. Then you carry wool till dusk. The pay is good, the ache is honest.}
opt.left.say.1 [51b95b] = {&你把橘子一筐筐扛上跳板，直到胳膊都忘了自己是胳膊。干完后工头付了钱，外加三个橘子。码头工人们不再咧嘴笑了，开始叫你的名字。|搬了一下午的桶。你趁没人看时用咒语浮起一只，工头看见了，什么也没说，多付了你一点。可你的背照样疼。|你念一句咒再推一把，吊车就不卡了，整个码头一片欢呼。然后你扛羊毛扛到黄昏。工钱不错，酸痛也实在。}
# en: Sit on a bollard and watch the ships
opt.right.label [de4021] = 坐在系缆桩上看船
# en: {&You sit on a bollard and watch ships from places you've only seen on maps unload things you can't name, and buy a hot pie and a bag of figs off every hawker who passes. It's a fine way to spend a day, and your purse.|The barrels go up, the gulls come down. You watch the whole thing with a pastry and a clear conscience, and then another pastry, and a third for the gull that's been staring at you.|You watch the northern ship unload, and the crane stick, and somebody else unstick it. You're happy. You've also bought a carved whale off a sailor for twice what it's worth.}
opt.right.say.1 [99f3a8] = {&你坐在系缆桩上，看着来自只在地图上见过的地方的船卸下叫不出名字的东西，每个路过的小贩手里你都买了热馅饼和一袋无花果。这么消磨一天真不错，钱包也跟着消磨了。|桶吊上去，海鸥落下来。你拿着一块点心，心安理得地看完了全程，又买了一块，再买第三块给那只一直盯着你的海鸥。|你看着北方的船卸货，看着吊车卡住，看着别人把它弄好。你很快乐。你还花两倍的价钱从一个水手手里买了一头木雕鲸鱼。}

@event docks_northern_ship
# en: Frost on the Rigging
title [b94790] = 索具上的霜
# en: A ship in from the far North is tied up on the quay, and though the morning is mild, there's frost on her rigging still, white to the crosstrees. Her sailors wear furs and say little. One old sailor sees your academy scarf and beckons. "Lumenhold," he says. "You want to buy a northern thing? Not cheap. Not safe either."
text [a418e9] = 一条从遥远北方来的船停在码头，早晨明明很暖和，她的索具上却还结着霜，一直白到桅顶横桁。船员们穿着毛皮，很少说话。一个老水手看见你的学院围巾，招了招手。“流明堡的，”他说，“想买件北方的东西吗？不便宜。也不安全。”
# en: A tall sailing ship at a harbour quay with frost thick on its rigging though the day is mild, northern sailors in furs unloading crates, one old sailor beckoning a student closer.
scene [982498] = 港口码头上一艘高大的帆船，天气温和，索具上却结满厚霜，穿毛皮的北方水手在卸箱子，一个老水手招呼一个学生靠近。
# en: See what he's selling
opt.left.label [28cf4b] = 看看他卖什么
# en: It's a lump of ice that doesn't melt, wrapped in sealskin, for "keeping things cold that should stay cold". In your room it frosts the window in a pattern like writing, and by the break's end it has melted to nothing, at last. Studying it, you learn more about cold than a term of lectures.
opt.left.say.1 [353312] = 是一块用海豹皮裹着的不化的冰，“用来让该冷的东西保持冷”。在你房间里，它把窗户冻出一片像字迹的花纹，到假期结束时终于化得一干二净。研究它的这些日子，你对寒冷的了解比一学期的课还多。
# en: Ask about the North instead
opt.right.label [4dc789] = 改问北方的事
# en: He tells you about the ice roads and the long night and the lights that sing over the glaciers, and he doesn't smile once. When he's done the mild morning feels thin, as if something had been let in. You walk away cold.
opt.right.say.1 [86af66] = 他给你讲冰路、长夜，还有在冰川上方歌唱的光，一次也没笑。他讲完后，温和的早晨显得单薄起来，像是有什么东西被放了进来。你走开时浑身发冷。

@event docks_undercroft_word
# en: Where the Dice Are
title [f2b958] = 骰子在哪儿
# en: A docker coming off shift jingles a dice-cup at you. "You play? Not here. Under the middle bridge, in the old cellars. The Undercroft. Cards, dice, a pit on fight nights. Bring coin, leave your wand in your pocket." He looks you over. "Or don't go. Smarter."
text [66bed7] = 一个刚下班的码头工人冲你晃了晃骰盅。“玩吗？不在这儿。在中桥底下，老地窖里。地下赌窟。牌、骰子，打擂的晚上还有个坑。带上钱，魔杖揣在兜里别拿出来。”他上下打量你。“要么就别去。更聪明。”
# en: A harbour tavern doorway at dusk, a weathered docker with a dice-cup leaning out to talk to a student, the arches of a great bridge visible upriver.
scene [3f457d] = 黄昏时港口酒馆的门口，一个饱经风霜、拿着骰盅的码头工人探出身和一个学生说话，上游远处能看见一座大桥的桥拱。
# en: Ask him the way in
opt.left.label [8669d3] = 问他怎么进去
# en: He draws it in spilled beer on a barrel-top: the third arch, the iron door, the word for the doorman. "Tell him the docks sent you," he says. Then he rubs the map out with his sleeve. You know the way now, and you know you shouldn't.
opt.left.say.1 [a94941] = 他用洒出来的啤酒在桶面上画给你：第三个桥拱，那扇铁门，给看门人的暗语。“就说是码头让你来的，”他说，然后用袖子把地图抹掉。你现在知道路了，也知道你不该去。
# en: Thank him and stay out of it
opt.right.label [4d12e7] = 谢过他，别掺和
# en: You thank him and walk on. "Third arch," he calls after you anyway, laughing, "iron door!" All the way home you look at the middle bridge, and wonder what's under it.
opt.right.say.1 [d4ae6d] = 你道了谢，继续走。“第三个桥拱，”他还是笑着在你身后喊，“铁门！”回家的一路上你都盯着中桥，想着它底下有什么。

@event docks_roof_runner
# en: Over the Roofs
title [8bc523] = 翻过屋顶
# en: Somebody drops off a low roof into the alley in front of you, a young woman in a patched coat, and two watchmen come pounding round the corner after her. "Leg up," she says to you, already reaching for the gutter. "Quick, and I'll show you the best view in the city."
text [632421] = 有人从低矮的屋顶跳进你面前的小巷，是个穿打补丁外套的年轻女人，两个巡警从拐角追了过来。“托我一把，”她对你说，手已经伸向檐沟，“快，我带你看全城最好的风景。”
# en: A narrow harbour alley, a young woman in a patched coat dropping off a low roof at a run with two watchmen behind her, a student in her path.
scene [4d45a5] = 狭窄的港口小巷，一个穿打补丁外套的年轻女人从低矮屋顶上一跃而下，身后两个巡警在追，一个学生挡在她的路上。
# en: Give her the leg up
opt.left.label [e7b391] = 托她一把
# en: You boost her, and she pulls you after, and you run over three streets of Port Calder's roofs without touching the ground, the watch shouting below. On a ridge by a chimney she stops, and the whole city's there in the dusk. "The Rookery," she says. "Don't tell." Then she's gone.
opt.left.say.1 [0f3e69] = 你托她上去，她又把你拉上去，你们在考尔德港的屋顶上跑过三条街，脚不沾地，巡警在下面大喊。她在一根烟囱旁的屋脊上停下，整座城市就在暮色里。“鸦巢，”她说，“别说出去。”然后她就不见了。
# en: Step aside for the watch
opt.right.label [bebd94] = 给巡警让路
# en: You step aside. She makes the gutter on her own, just, and turns on the ridge to shout down at you, "The Rookery! Come and see it, coward!" The watchmen thank you. You feel righteous, and also as if you'd been shown a way up and stayed on the ground.
opt.right.say.1 [93ef6d] = 你让开了。她自己勉强够到了檐沟，在屋脊上回头冲你喊：“鸦巢！有胆就来看看，胆小鬼！”巡警们向你道谢。你觉得自己做得对，又觉得像是有人给你指了一条往上的路，你却留在了地面。

@event shop_fish_market
# en: The Fish Market's Barrows
title [524f24] = 鱼市的推车
# en: {~The fish market is all ice, shouting and gulls, and the barrows at the end of the quay feed the people who've been up since three: chowder, hot pasties, oysters on a plate of seaweed.|The barrows steam at the quay's end. A fishwife ladles chowder with one hand and fights off a gull with the other.}
text [94e460] = {~鱼市满是冰块、吆喝和海鸥，码头尽头的推车供应凌晨三点就起床的人吃喝：杂鱼浓汤、热馅饼、铺在海藻上的生蚝。|码头尽头的推车冒着热气。一个卖鱼妇一只手舀浓汤，另一只手赶海鸥。}
# en: A dawn quay market of fish on ice, gulls on every roof, barrows steaming with hot food, a fishwife ladling soup for a student.
scene [ed3418] = 黎明时码头上的鱼市，冰上摆着鱼，每个屋顶上都有海鸥，推车冒着热食的蒸汽，一个卖鱼妇正给一个学生舀汤。
# en: A bowl of quay chowder
opt.chowder.label [ae8867] = 一碗码头浓汤
# en: Health; it ends a hungry month.
opt.chowder.hint [f3d661] = 健康；能结束挨饿的一个月。
# en: {~Chowder thick enough to stand a spoon in, and a heel of bread to fight the gulls for. You eat it on the quay wall with the dockers, and you're warm to the toes.|The fishwife puts in extra mussels "for the scarf". You eat it standing, scalding your mouth, very happy.}
opt.chowder.say.1 [82f36e] = {~浓得能立住勺子的杂鱼汤，配一块得和海鸥抢的面包。你和码头工人一起坐在码头墙上吃，从头暖到脚。|卖鱼妇“看在围巾的份上”多给你加了贻贝。你站着吃，烫了嘴，开心极了。}
# en: A dozen oysters at the stand
opt.oysters.label [2d7f9b] = 在摊上来一打生蚝
# en: Mood, and a little Health.
opt.oysters.hint [435f7c] = 心情，外加少许健康。
# en: {~A dozen on seaweed, a squeeze of lemon. The oyster-man opens them faster than you can eat them, and calls you a lord for paying.|You eat them watching the boats come in, and the oyster-man tells you which bay each one's from, as if introducing them.}
opt.oysters.say.1 [7d2298] = {~一打摆在海藻上，挤一点柠檬。卖生蚝的人开得比你吃得还快，因为你付了钱，管你叫老爷。|你一边看渔船进港一边吃，卖生蚝的人告诉你每一只来自哪个海湾，像在介绍客人。}
# en: Buy a fishwife a cup and listen
opt.gossip.label [230730] = 请卖鱼妇喝杯茶，听她说
# en: The quay's gossip: Lore, and the city's news before it's printed.
opt.gossip.hint [be96c1] = 码头的八卦：学识，还有见报之前的城中新闻。
# en: {~For the price of a cup of tea, a fishwife tells you who drowned, who eloped, which ship's late and why, all before breakfast. Printing Row will have it by dusk, wrong.|The fishwives tell you the bonded warehouses doubled their dogs. They tell you everything. You realise they'll tell everyone about you, too.}
opt.gossip.say.1 [21ea88] = {~一杯茶的价钱，卖鱼妇就在早饭前告诉你谁淹死了、谁私奔了、哪条船晚了以及为什么。印刷街要到黄昏才会登出来，还是错的。|卖鱼妇们告诉你保税仓库的狗加了一倍。她们什么都告诉你。你这才意识到，她们也会把你的事告诉所有人。}
# en: Walk the quay and smell the sea
opt.look.label [e84613] = 沿码头走走，闻闻海的味道
# en: {~You walk the length of the quay past the ice and the shouting, and buy nothing, and smell of fish till noon.|The gulls follow you the whole way, sure you've got something. You haven't.}
opt.look.say.1 [67b9b8] = {~你沿着码头走过冰块和吆喝声，什么也没买，一身鱼味直到中午。|海鸥一路跟着你，笃定你身上有吃的。你没有。}

@event fish_market_auction
# en: The Late-Boat Auction
title [d21a9c] = 晚船拍卖
# en: When the late boats come in, the auction is held by hand-signals, too fast to follow: a finger is a crown, a tug of the ear is ten, and a scratch of the nose has ruined people. The auctioneer's on his crate. A whole crate of mackerel is going cheap, if you can bid without buying the boat by mistake.
text [00c75c] = 晚归的渔船一靠岸，拍卖就靠手势进行，快得根本跟不上：一根手指是一克朗，揪一下耳朵是十克朗，挠一下鼻子曾让人倾家荡产。拍卖师站上了箱子。一整箱鲭鱼正便宜出手，前提是你能出价而不小心买下一条船。
# en: A crowded midday fish auction on a quay, buyers in aprons making tiny hand signals at an auctioneer on a crate, crates of silver fish on ice, a student with a hand half-raised.
scene [ce4414] = 正午码头上拥挤的鱼类拍卖，系着围裙的买家对站在箱子上的拍卖师做着细小的手势，冰上一箱箱银光闪闪的鱼，一个学生的手举到一半。
# en: Bid for the crate
opt.left.label [09b9cf] = 竞拍那箱鱼
# en: Pay for the crate, and sell it on.
opt.left.hint [03762b] = 买下这箱鱼，再转手卖掉。
# en: You keep your hands in your pockets till the last moment and take the crate with one finger, and pay for it out of your purse. Within the hour you sell it on to a barrow for twice what you paid. The auctioneer winks at you. The buyers pretend not to have noticed you.
opt.left.say.1 [a13344] = 你一直把手揣在兜里，直到最后一刻才伸出一根手指拿下那箱鱼，从钱袋里付了钱。不到一个钟头，你就以两倍的价钱转卖给了一辆推车。拍卖师冲你眨了眨眼。买家们假装没注意到你。
# en: You scratch your nose. You've paid for a crate of mackerel, a crate of herring, and very nearly a boat. You sell them on for less than you paid, smelling of fish, and the buyers clap you on the back.
opt.left.say.2 [d77c3c] = 你挠了挠鼻子。你付钱买下了一箱鲭鱼、一箱鲱鱼，还差点买下一条船。你赔本转卖了它们，一身鱼腥，买家们拍着你的背。
# en: Watch the hands
opt.right.label [d27bb5] = 盯着那些手
# en: You stand on a bollard and watch nothing but the buyers' hands for an hour. By the end you can follow the auction, just, and you've learned that the quietest buyer in the market is the one who owns it. Your feet are frozen.
opt.right.say.1 [a90bb1] = 你站在系缆桩上，一个小时只盯着买家们的手。到最后你勉强能跟上拍卖了，还发现鱼市里最安静的那个买家就是鱼市的主人。你的脚冻僵了。

@event fish_market_gull_war
# en: The Gull War
title [e2385e] = 海鸥战争
# en: The fish market is at war with the gulls, and today the gulls are winning. Their general is a huge one-eyed bird the fishwives call the bishop, for the way he blesses the barrows, and he has just taken a whole salmon off a barrow and is standing on it, daring anyone. The fishwives look at you. "Wizard," says one. "Do something."
text [649cab] = 鱼市正和海鸥打仗，而今天海鸥占了上风。它们的将军是一只巨大的独眼海鸥，卖鱼妇们管它叫“主教”，因为它总在推车上“赐福”。它刚从推车上叼走一整条鲑鱼，正站在上面，看谁敢来。卖鱼妇们看向你。“巫师，”一个说，“想想办法。”
# en: A fish market quay under attack by a mob of gulls, fishwives swinging brooms, a huge one-eyed gull on a barrow holding a whole fish, a student caught in the middle.
scene [314edb] = 遭海鸥群袭击的鱼市码头，卖鱼妇们挥舞扫帚，一只巨大的独眼海鸥站在推车上守着一整条鱼，一个学生夹在中间。
# en: Drive the gulls off with a spell
opt.left.label [017f89] = 用咒语赶走海鸥
# en: A clap of light and wind sends the whole flock up off the quay at once. The one-eyed gull goes last, without the salmon, and gives you a look that promises a long war. The fishwives give you the salmon.
opt.left.say.1 [5d6797] = 一声光与风的炸响，整群海鸥同时从码头上腾空而起。独眼海鸥最后一个飞走，没带走鲑鱼，临走瞪了你一眼，预示着一场持久战。卖鱼妇们把鲑鱼送给了你。
# en: Your spell scatters the fishwives. The gulls stay. The one-eyed gull finishes the salmon and is sick on your boot, deliberately, you're sure of it.
opt.left.say.2 [34058b] = 你的咒语把卖鱼妇们吓散了。海鸥没动。独眼海鸥吃完了鲑鱼，然后吐在你的靴子上——你确信是故意的。
# en: Bribe the general
opt.right.label [572c46] = 贿赂将军
# en: You buy a herring and offer it, very respectfully, to the one-eyed gull. He considers it, takes it, and leads the whole flock off to the roofs. The fishwives call it shameful. It's a truce. It lasts till noon.
opt.right.say.1 [25ca77] = 你买了一条鲱鱼，毕恭毕敬地献给独眼海鸥。它考虑了一下，收下了，领着整群海鸥飞回了屋顶。卖鱼妇们说这真丢人。这是一份停战协议。它持续到中午。

@event fish_market_golden_fish
# en: Throw It Back
title [3b92d3] = 放回去
# en: On a barrow at the end of the quay, among the silver, lies a small fish with scales like coins. The fishwives won't touch it. "That one goes back," says the oldest. "Always. My gran's gran said so." She lifts it in her apron and puts it into your hands. "You're the stranger. You do it." A buyer from uptown is already waving a fistful of money at you for it.
text [516b1d] = 码头尽头的一辆推车上，一堆银鱼当中，躺着一条鳞片像硬币一样的小鱼。卖鱼妇们谁也不肯碰它。“那条得放回去，”最年长的那位说，“一向如此。我奶奶的奶奶说的。”她用围裙把它托起来，放进你手里。“你是外乡人。你来。”一个上城来的买家已经冲你挥着一把钱要买它了。
# en: A fish market stall at dawn, a small fish with golden scales gasping on the ice, old fishwives gathered around it uneasily, one holding out the fish to a student.
scene [0a9cdf] = 黎明时鱼市的一个摊位，一条金鳞小鱼在冰上喘息，年老的卖鱼妇们不安地围着它，其中一位把鱼递向一个学生。
# en: Throw it back yourself
opt.left.label [e5b8a8] = 亲手把它放回去
# en: You carry it in your cupped hands to the quay's end and let it go into the grey water. It turns once, a flash of gold, and is gone. The fishwives nod. That night you dream of coins under the sea, quietly, and wake rested.
opt.left.say.1 [542681] = 你双手捧着它走到码头尽头，把它放进灰色的海水。它转了一圈，金光一闪，就不见了。卖鱼妇们点点头。那天夜里你安安静静地梦见海底的硬币，醒来时神清气爽。
# en: Sell it to the uptown buyer
opt.right.label [520b66] = 卖给上城的买家
# en: The buyer pays you for it, in front of the fishwives, and carries it off for his aquarium. The fishwives turn their backs on you. Nothing happens. Nothing happens all break, and you can't stop waiting for it.
opt.right.say.1 [21d42d] = 买家当着卖鱼妇们的面付了钱，把它带回去养在鱼缸里。卖鱼妇们背过身去。什么也没发生。整个假期什么也没发生，你却忍不住一直在等。

@event coaching_yard_arrivals
# en: The Coach Is In
title [deae1d] = 马车到了
# en: {&A coach from the north rolls in spattered to the windows, and the yard fills with trunks, horses, porters and people trying to remember which trunk is theirs. An old woman holds out a parcel. "Can you carry this to the Crescent, dear? I'll pay."|The coach from the coast, late and muddy. A clerk with a parcel he can't leave the yard to deliver looks at you hopefully.|The mail coach swings in with its horn blowing. The guard tosses down a sack of letters, and one parcel addressed in a hand that's clearly urgent.}
text [f343a6] = {&一辆从北方来的马车驶进院子，泥一直溅到车窗，院子里顿时挤满了箱子、马匹、搬运工，还有努力回想哪只箱子是自己的人。一位老太太递过来一个包裹。“能帮我送到新月街吗，孩子？我付钱。”|海边来的马车，晚点了，满身是泥。一个离不开院子的文员拿着一个包裹，满怀希望地看着你。|邮车吹着号角转进院子。押车人扔下一袋信，还有一个笔迹明显很急的包裹。}
# en: A busy coaching inn yard, a mud-spattered coach just arrived, porters unloading trunks, travellers milling, an anxious old traveller holding a parcel out to a student.
scene [7de2e6] = 繁忙的驿车场，一辆满是泥点的马车刚到，搬运工在卸箱子，旅客们来来往往，一位焦急的老旅客把一个包裹递向一个学生。
# en: Carry the parcel across the city
opt.left.label [9ff6a1] = 穿城送包裹
# en: {&The Crescent is at the top of the steepest hill in the capital. You deliver the parcel to a butler who signs for it with tremendous gravity. The old woman pays you double. Your legs complain all evening.|You carry the clerk's parcel to a counting house in Port Calder, the far end of the city, and get paid at both ends. You're footsore.|You run the urgent parcel to a doctor's door in midtown. He pays you, and then runs, too. You never find out what was in it. Your feet ache.}
opt.left.say.1 [f66a82] = {&新月街在王都最陡的那座山顶上。你把包裹交给一位庄重异常地签收的管家。老太太付了你双倍。你的腿抱怨了一整晚。|你把文员的包裹送到城市另一头考尔德港的一家账房，两头都收了钱。你的脚走疼了。|你把那个急件跑送到中城一位医生的门口。他付了钱，然后也跑了。你永远不知道里面是什么。你的脚很疼。}
# en: Help the porters with the trunks
opt.right.label [bf1282] = 帮搬运工搬箱子
# en: {&Trunks, hatboxes, a birdcage and somebody's harp. The porters let you carry the harp. By the end your arms ache and you know every hotel in the city.|You heave trunks off the roof of the coach with the porters, who are delighted to have a wizard who doesn't use magic. By the end, you wish you had.|Mail sacks, trunks, a crate that growls. You leave the crate to the porters. You carry everything else, and ache for it.}
opt.right.say.1 [95f942] = {&箱子、帽盒、一只鸟笼，还有不知谁的竖琴。搬运工让你搬竖琴。到最后你的胳膊酸了，城里每家旅馆你都知道了。|你和搬运工一起把箱子从车顶上卸下来，他们很高兴遇到一个不用魔法的巫师。到最后，你倒希望自己用了。|邮袋、箱子、一只会低吼的板条箱。板条箱留给搬运工。其余的都是你搬的，酸痛也是你的。}

@event coaching_yard_wrong_trunk
# en: The Wrong Trunk
title [5eddf3] = 错的箱子
# en: In the bustle of the yard you see a porter in a cap that doesn't fit him swap the label on a fine leather trunk for a scruffy one, and wheel the fine one briskly towards the gate. Its owner, a flustered governess off the coast coach, is still searching the pile for it. Nobody else has noticed. The gate is twenty yards away.
text [7343c6] = 院子里一片忙乱，你看见一个戴着不合头的帽子的搬运工把一只精致皮箱上的标签和一只破箱子的对调了，然后推着那只精致的快步朝大门走去。箱子的主人，一位从海边马车上下来、手忙脚乱的家庭女教师，还在箱子堆里找它。没人注意到。大门在二十码外。
# en: A coaching yard with trunks piled high, a smooth porter in a borrowed cap wheeling away a fine trunk on a barrow, a flustered traveller searching the pile, a student watching.
scene [21016d] = 堆满箱子的驿车场，一个戴着借来帽子的油滑搬运工正用推车推走一只精致的箱子，一位手忙脚乱的旅客在箱子堆里翻找，一个学生在一旁看着。
# en: Go after the porter
opt.left.label [5ba872] = 去追那个搬运工
# en: You catch him at the gate and put a hand on the barrow. He looks at your wand, decides against it, and runs, leaving the trunk. The governess nearly weeps; everything she owns is in it. She insists on giving you a coin, and a lecture on punctuality.
opt.left.say.1 [bd944e] = 你在大门口追上他，一手按住推车。他看看你的魔杖，打消了念头，扔下箱子跑了。家庭女教师差点哭出来；她所有的家当都在里面。她坚持要给你一枚硬币，外加一通关于守时的训诫。
# en: You catch him at the gate, and he shoves you into a horse trough and is gone into the street with the trunk. The governess helps you out, which is kind of her, considering. You're soaked and bruised, and her trunk is gone.
opt.left.say.2 [5c268d] = 你在大门口追上他，他把你推进饮马槽，带着箱子消失在街上。家庭女教师把你拉了出来，考虑到情况，她真是好心。你浑身湿透、满身瘀青，她的箱子也没了。
# en: Tell the yard-master
opt.right.label [bf1194] = 告诉驿车场总管
# en: You find the yard-master, who finds the constable, who finds the barrow in an alley with the trunk forced open and half its contents gone. The governess thanks you for trying. It was the sensible thing, and it was too slow.
opt.right.say.1 [fd9b3a] = 你找到驿车场总管，总管找来警员，警员在一条小巷里找到了推车，箱子被撬开，东西少了一半。家庭女教师谢谢你尽了力。这是明智的做法，只是太慢了。

@event coaching_yard_travellers_tale
# en: Off the Southern Coach
title [e9c33d] = 南来的马车
# en: The southern coach brings a sun-browned traveller with a battered trunk covered in labels from a dozen ports. In the coaching inn's taproom he's telling the whole room about a city where the streets are canals and the wizards wear masks to work. He wants an audience, and a drink.
text [1ef2cc] = 南来的马车载来一个晒得黝黑的旅人，他那只破旧的箱子上贴满了十几个港口的标签。在驿站客栈的酒馆里，他正给满屋子的人讲一座街道都是运河、巫师戴着面具上班的城市。他想要听众，还想要一杯酒。
# en: A coaching inn's crowded taproom, a sun-browned traveller with a battered trunk telling a story to a ring of listeners, a student leaning in.
scene [f58ee1] = 驿站客栈拥挤的酒馆，一个晒得黝黑、带着破旧箱子的旅人正给一圈听众讲故事，一个学生探身倾听。
# en: Buy him a drink and listen
opt.left.label [f48648] = 请他喝一杯，听他讲
# en: You buy him a drink, and he tells you the whole south: the canal city, the masked wizards, a market that floats and a duel fought in gondolas. Some of it is even true, probably. You walk home with your head full of water and lanterns.
opt.left.say.1 [d1f8a2] = 你请他喝了一杯，他给你讲了整个南方：运河之城，戴面具的巫师，一座漂浮的集市，一场在贡多拉上进行的决斗。有些甚至可能是真的。你回家时满脑子都是水和灯笼。
# en: Tell him about Lumenhold instead
opt.right.label [47f577] = 改给他讲流明堡
# en: You tell him about a castle on a lake, moving staircases and a cat who files the library. He's delighted, and writes it all in a little book for his next audience. You realise, walking home, that you've just become somebody's traveller's tale, and you miss the castle.
opt.right.say.1 [f4b6c3] = 你给他讲湖上的城堡、会动的楼梯，还有一只给图书馆归档的猫。他高兴极了，把这些都记进一个小本子，留着讲给下一批听众。回家的路上你意识到，你刚刚变成了别人口中的旅人故事，你想念城堡了。

@event cathedral_under_the_lamp
# en: Under the Lamp
title [31e340] = 明灯之下
# en: {&The cathedral swallows the city's noise at the door. High over the altar the Lamp burns, as it has for four hundred years, and the light it gives is warmer than it has any right to be.|The Lamp burns steady over an empty nave. A verger is trimming the candles below it, very slowly, as if there were all the time in the world.|The city's too loud today, and the nave is cool. The Lamp burns, and a choir somewhere is rehearsing one phrase over and over.}
text [7fbd4e] = {&大教堂在门口就吞没了城市的喧嚣。祭坛上方高处，明灯燃烧着，四百年来一直如此，它的光温暖得不合常理。|明灯在空荡荡的中殿上方稳稳燃烧。一位司事在灯下修剪蜡烛，非常慢，仿佛世上有的是时间。|今天城里太吵，中殿很凉。明灯燃烧着，某处有个唱诗班在一遍又一遍地排练同一句。}
# en: The vast nave of a cathedral, a great lamp burning high over the altar, warm golden light, a student sitting alone on a pew, a few worshippers kneeling.
scene [023a49] = 大教堂宏伟的中殿，祭坛上方高处燃着一盏巨大的灯，温暖的金光，一个学生独自坐在长椅上，几位信众跪着。
# en: Sit under the Lamp a while
opt.left.label [5071ba] = 在明灯下坐一会儿
# en: {&You light a candle under the Lamp, a few coins in the box, and sit an hour in the warm light thinking about nothing at all. You come out lighter.|You buy a candle from the verger and sit and watch him trim the others. It takes him an hour. It's the most restful hour of the break.|You put a coin in the choir's box on the way in and sit while they get the phrase right at last, and the whole nave rings with it.}
opt.left.say.1 [017cef] = {&你往箱子里投了几枚硬币，在明灯下点了一支蜡烛，在温暖的光里坐了一个小时，什么也不想。出来时你轻松了。|你向司事买了一支蜡烛，坐着看他修剪其他的蜡烛。他花了一个小时。这是整个假期最安宁的一个小时。|进门时你往唱诗班的箱子里投了一枚硬币，一直坐到他们终于唱对了那一句，整个中殿都随之回响。}
# en: Read the old memorials
opt.right.label [97566c] = 读那些古老的纪念铭文
# en: {&The walls are thick with brass memorials: drowned admirals, a bishop who saw a dragon, a lamplighter who kept the Lamp lit through the great flood. You read them all, and come out a little sad.|You read the floor, the old names worn smooth by four hundred years of feet. Most of them were young.|You find a memorial to a Lumenhold student, two hundred years ago, "who loved the city and was lost in it". You stand in front of it a long time.}
opt.right.say.1 [10a285] = {&墙上密密麻麻全是铜质纪念牌：淹死的海军将领，一位见过龙的主教，一个在大洪水中让明灯一直亮着的点灯人。你全都读了，出来时有点伤感。|你读地面上那些被四百年的脚步磨平的古老名字。他们大多都很年轻。|你找到一块两百年前一位流明堡学生的纪念牌，“他爱这座城，也迷失在了这座城里”。你在它面前站了很久。}

@event cathedral_crypt_archive
# en: The Crypt Archive
title [a7a836] = 地穴档案
# en: Under the cathedral, among the tombs, is an archive older than the Royal Library's: four hundred years of baptisms, burials and the bishops' private letters. The archivist, who is nearly as old as some of it, will let a scholar in for an hour, for a donation to the Lamp, or for a morning's copying.
text [a15bc7] = 大教堂底下，在一座座坟墓之间，有一个比皇家图书馆还古老的档案馆：四百年的洗礼、葬礼记录和主教们的私人信件。档案员老得快和其中一些档案一样了，他会让学者进去待一个小时，条件是给明灯捐一笔钱，或者抄写一上午。
# en: A vaulted cathedral crypt lined with shelves of ancient ledgers and scrolls, a very old archivist with a candle leading a student between the tombs.
scene [109c9e] = 大教堂拱顶地穴里排满古老账册和卷轴的书架，一位非常年老的档案员举着蜡烛领一个学生穿过坟墓之间。
# en: Make a donation and read
opt.left.label [29c4f5] = 捐一笔钱，进去读
# en: An hour among the bishops' letters, by candle: quarrels with kings, a recipe for the Lamp's oil, a love letter nobody burned. You come up blinking into the nave with a head full of the city's oldest secrets, and lighter in the purse.
opt.left.say.1 [d298fc] = 在主教们的信件中间就着烛光待了一个小时：与国王的争吵，明灯灯油的配方，一封没人烧掉的情书。你眨着眼回到中殿，满脑子都是这座城最古老的秘密，钱袋也轻了。
# en: Copy a ledger for him
opt.right.label [1ca741] = 替他抄一本账册
# en: The archivist sets you to copying a burial register that's falling apart. Four hours of cramped names by candlelight in the cold. He checks every line, says "Legible," and lets you read one letter of your choice. Your back and your eyes are sore.
opt.right.say.1 [2868a5] = 档案员让你抄写一本快散架的葬礼登记簿。在寒冷里就着烛光抄了四个小时密密麻麻的名字。他逐行检查，说了声“认得出”，让你挑一封信读。你的背和眼睛都酸了。

@event cathedral_ringing_chamber
# en: The Ringing Chamber
title [0955b0] = 鸣钟室
# en: Up a stair of three hundred steps is the cathedral's ringing chamber, a circle of ropes with striped grips hanging from the dark. The ringers are one short for the full peal the city expects on a saint's day, and the tower captain has come down to the nave to find anybody with strong arms. He hands you a rope. "Pull when I say. Let go when I say. Never otherwise."
text [b41a24] = 爬上三百级台阶，就是大教堂的鸣钟室，一圈握柄带条纹的绳子从黑暗中垂下来。今天是圣徒纪念日，全城都等着听完整的一轮变奏钟声，可敲钟人少了一个，钟楼领班下到中殿来找有力气的人。他递给你一根绳子。“我说拉就拉。我说放就放。别的时候都不行。”
# en: A cathedral bell-ringing chamber high in a tower, a circle of bell ropes with striped grips, ringers in shirtsleeves, a tower captain holding out a rope to a student.
scene [0a1504] = 大教堂钟楼高处的鸣钟室，一圈握柄带条纹的钟绳，只穿衬衫的敲钟人，一位钟楼领班把一根绳子递给一个学生。
# en: Ring the peal
opt.left.label [c7a102] = 敲完这一轮
# en: Three hours of pull and let go, in time with seven strangers, while the whole tower shakes and the capital below hears every change. When the last bell stops the ringers clap you on the back and write your name in the peal book, in ink.
opt.left.say.1 [c4b50c] = 三个小时的拉和放，和七个陌生人保持节拍，整座钟楼都在震动，下面的王都听得见每一次变换。最后一口钟停下时，敲钟人们拍着你的背，用墨水把你的名字写进了钟谱簿。
# en: You pull when he doesn't say, and the rope takes you up off your feet towards the ceiling before you let go. The captain catches the rope, and the peal, and you, in that order. You sit out the rest on the bench with rope-burned hands.
opt.left.say.2 [009732] = 他没说拉你就拉了，绳子把你整个人吊离地面往天花板上拽，你才松手。领班依次接住了绳子、钟声和你。你手上带着绳子勒出的伤，在长凳上坐完了剩下的时间。
# en: Climb on up to the spire
opt.right.label [9f1a01] = 接着往上爬到尖塔
# en: You leave the ringers to it and climb on, up past the bells to a little room under the spire where the window looks out over the whole city to the sea. The bells start below you and the floor hums. Your legs ache all the way back down.
opt.right.say.1 [f5d9e9] = 你把钟交给敲钟人，接着往上爬，经过一口口钟，来到尖塔下的一个小房间，窗外是整座城市，一直到海。钟声在你脚下响起，地板嗡嗡作响。下来的一路上你的腿都在疼。

@event cathedral_sanctuary
# en: Sanctuary
title [849509] = 庇护
# en: At dusk a young man runs up the cathedral steps and grabs the great iron ring on the door, two bailiffs behind him. Whoever holds the ring has sanctuary, the old law says, but the bailiffs are already climbing, and the verger is nowhere. "Debt," the young man gasps. "Just debt. Please."
text [851fc5] = 黄昏时，一个年轻人跑上大教堂的台阶，一把抓住门上的大铁环，身后跟着两个法警。古老的法律说，握住铁环的人就受庇护，可法警已经在往上爬了，司事却不见踪影。“是债，”年轻人喘着气说，“只是欠债。求你了。”
# en: A cathedral's great door at dusk, a desperate young man clinging to the iron door-ring, two bailiffs on the steps below, a student standing in the doorway.
scene [28f9e8] = 黄昏时大教堂的巨门，一个绝望的年轻人紧抓着铁门环，两个法警在下面的台阶上，一个学生站在门口。
# en: Stand between him and the bailiffs
opt.left.label [309c95] = 挡在他和法警之间
# en: You stand in the doorway with your wand out and recite the old law at the bailiffs, word for word, until the verger comes running. The bailiffs leave, swearing, and one of them shoves you into the doorpost on the way. The young man has sanctuary, and you have a bruise.
opt.left.say.1 [7cdcd7] = 你拿着魔杖站在门口，一字一句地向法警背诵那条古老的法律，直到司事跑了过来。法警骂骂咧咧地走了，其中一个经过时把你推到门柱上。年轻人得到了庇护，你得到了一块瘀青。
# en: Pay his debt
opt.right.label [04110e] = 替他还债
# en: "How much?" you ask the bailiffs. They tell you. It's more than you'd like and less than a life. You count it into the sergeant's hand on the cathedral steps, and the young man lets go of the ring and sits down on the step and cries. You walk home a good deal lighter.
opt.right.say.1 [ae93e4] = “多少钱？”你问法警。他们说了数。比你希望的多，比一条命少。你在大教堂的台阶上把钱数进警长手里，年轻人松开铁环，坐在台阶上哭了。你走回家时，钱袋轻了许多，心里也是。

@event printing_row_broadsheets
# en: Hot Off the Press
title [45d281] = 刚出炉的报纸
# en: {&Printing Row thumps like a heart. Every door has a press behind it and every press is printing something somebody will regret. A printer's devil runs past shouting tomorrow's headline today.|Printing Row smells of ink and hot metal. A broadsheet headline in letters a hand high: SCANDAL AT THE CLUB.|Printing Row at full roar. Two rival broadsheets are printing the same story with opposite endings, and selling both from the same corner.}
text [388994] = {&印刷街像一颗心脏一样砰砰跳动。每扇门后都有一台印刷机，每台印刷机都在印某人日后会后悔的东西。一个印刷学徒跑过，喊着明天的头条。|印刷街满是油墨和热金属的气味。一张大报的标题字有一掌高：俱乐部丑闻。|印刷街正全速轰鸣。两家对头的大报印着同一个故事，结局相反，在同一个街角一起叫卖。}
# en: A narrow street of printing presses, ink-stained printers' devils running with bundles of fresh broadsheets, a student buying a damp sheet from a boy on a corner.
scene [fcf360] = 一条满是印刷机的窄街，满手油墨的印刷学徒抱着成捆的新报奔跑，一个学生正从街角的报童手里买一张还潮着的报纸。
# en: Buy every broadsheet on the Row
opt.left.label [7fe3bf] = 把这条街上的报纸全买下
# en: {&You read them all on a step, ink coming off on your fingers: a duel, a drowned ship, a minister's debts, an advertisement for a hair tonic with a lion in it. You know the capital better by the end, and believe less of it.|You read about the club scandal in five versions. In three of them the guilty party is a duke. In one it's the porter.|You read both endings of the same story and decide, on balance, that neither happened. You know a great deal of nonsense now, and some of it is true.}
opt.left.say.1 [b2f36c] = {&你坐在台阶上把它们全读了，油墨沾了一手：一场决斗，一条沉船，一位大臣的债务，一则配着狮子的生发水广告。读完后你更了解王都了，也更不信它了。|你读了俱乐部丑闻的五个版本。其中三个说罪魁是一位公爵。有一个说是门房。|你读完了同一个故事的两个结局，权衡之后认定两个都没发生过。你现在知道了大量胡说八道，其中有些是真的。}
# en: Sell them a story
opt.right.label [501f0b] = 卖给他们一个故事
# en: {&You tell an editor about a gull that steals salmon at the fish market. He buys it, and by dusk it's a sea monster. Your name is spelt wrong in the paper, which is probably for the best.|You sell a story about a ghost at the theatre. The paper prints it as an omen. People at the theatre now look at you oddly.|You sell a story about a student who can walk through walls. They print it about somebody else entirely, and pay you anyway.}
opt.right.say.1 [1e7282] = {&你给一位编辑讲鱼市上偷鲑鱼的海鸥。他买了，到黄昏它就成了海怪。报上你的名字拼错了，这大概是好事。|你卖了一个剧院闹鬼的故事。报纸把它当成预兆登了出来。现在剧院里的人看你的眼神都有点怪。|你卖了一个关于能穿墙的学生的故事。他们登的是完全不相干的另一个人，照样付了你钱。}
# en: {&The editor listens, yawns, and says he had it yesterday, better.|"Nobody believes academy students," the editor says. "That's what makes them news, but not today."|The editor buys nothing, and then prints your story anyway, under a rival's name. You can't prove it.}
opt.right.say.2 [7c1295] = {&编辑听着，打了个哈欠，说他昨天就有了，还更好。|“没人信学院学生的话，”编辑说，“所以他们才有新闻价值，但不是今天。”|编辑什么也没买，然后照样把你的故事登了出来，署的是对手的名字。你证明不了。}

@event printing_row_your_name
# en: Your Name in Print
title [944d73] = 你的名字上了报
# en: In a printing shop on the Row a proof sheet is drying on the line, and your own name is in the headline: something you did at the academy, told badly and made worse, ready for the morning edition. The editor smirks. "Unless," he says, "you'd care to give us something better."
text [f0b111] = 印刷街的一家铺子里，一张校样正晾在绳子上，标题里赫然是你的名字：你在学院做过的某件事，讲得很糟，又被添油加醋，正等着上明天的早报。编辑得意地笑着。“除非，”他说，“你愿意给我们一个更好的故事。”
# en: A printing shop, a printer holding up a wet proof sheet, a student reading their own name in the headline with alarm, an editor smirking behind them.
scene [7fa8e0] = 一家印刷铺里，印刷工举着一张湿漉漉的校样，一个学生惊恐地看着标题里自己的名字，编辑在身后得意地笑着。
# en: Give him a better story
opt.left.label [63519c] = 给他一个更好的故事
# en: You give him a better story, true but sharper, about somebody else. He tears down your proof and sets theirs. In the morning the city's talking about you anyway, kindly this time, and about them, not kindly at all.
opt.left.say.1 [8abbe8] = 你给了他一个更好的故事，真实但更尖锐，主角是别人。他撕下你的校样，排上了那个人的。第二天早上全城照样在谈论你，这回是好话；也在谈论那个人，一句好话也没有。
# en: Let them print it
opt.right.label [9c34b8] = 让他们印
# en: You tell him to print and be damned. He does. In the morning the whole capital reads the worst version of you over breakfast, and a fishwife at the quay asks if it's true. You tell her it isn't, quite, and find you can live with that.
opt.right.say.1 [30998e] = 你让他尽管印，爱怎么印怎么印。他真印了。第二天早上全王都都在早餐桌上读到了最糟版本的你，码头上一个卖鱼妇问你是不是真的。你告诉她不完全是，然后发现自己也能接受。

@event printing_row_jammed_press
# en: The Jammed Press
title [6ce8ed] = 卡住的印刷机
# en: A great iron press has jammed in a shop on the Row halfway through the evening edition, with a broadsheet chewed up in its jaws and four hundred more to go. The printer, inky to the shoulders, sees your academy scarf through the window and comes out into the street after you. "Can you fix machines? Can you fix anything? Please?"
text [e6aca7] = 印刷街一家铺子里，一台巨大的铁印刷机在晚报印到一半时卡住了，钳口里嚼着一张皱巴巴的报纸，还有四百张要印。油墨一直沾到肩膀的印刷工透过窗户看见了你的学院围巾，追到街上来。“你会修机器吗？你什么都能修吗？求你了？”
# en: A printing shop in chaos, a big iron press jammed mid-edition with paper crumpled in its jaws, a frantic printer with inky hands waving a student over, stacks of half-printed broadsheets.
scene [75eb88] = 一片混乱的印刷铺，一台大铁印刷机在印报中途卡住，钳口里卡着揉皱的纸，一个满手油墨的焦急印刷工招呼一个学生过去，周围堆着印了一半的报纸。
# en: Work it by hand with him
opt.left.label [15c33b] = 和他一起手工印
# en: You and the printer clear the jaws, ink the forme by hand and pull the edition one sheet at a time, all four hundred, on the old hand-lever. By dusk you're black to the elbows and your shoulders are on fire, and the papers are on the street. He pays you in coin and a copy.
opt.left.say.1 [91d81a] = 你和印刷工清理了钳口，手工给版面上墨，用老式手摇杆一张一张地印完了整批报纸，整整四百张。到黄昏你从手到肘全是黑的，肩膀火烧火燎，报纸上了街。他付了你钱，还送你一份。
# en: Coax the press with a spell
opt.right.label [61b53b] = 用咒语哄好印刷机
# en: You find the bent pin in the gearing by feel and a word, and ease it straight. The press shudders, groans and starts again, faster than before. The printer pays you double and puts your name in the edition's corner, very small, for luck.
opt.right.say.1 [ec0cd8] = 你凭手感和一句咒语找到齿轮里那根弯了的销子，把它慢慢掰直。印刷机一阵颤抖，呻吟着重新转了起来，比原来还快。印刷工付了双倍，还在这期报纸的角落里印上你的名字，很小，图个吉利。
# en: Your spell unjams the press, and it runs, and runs, and won't stop, and prints the same page two hundred times before the printer gets a crowbar into it. He pays you nothing, and you go home with ink in your hair.
opt.right.say.2 [4ec448] = 你的咒语让印刷机动了起来，它转啊转，停不下来，把同一页印了两百遍，印刷工才用撬棍把它别住。他一分钱也没付，你回家时头发里都是油墨。

@event undercroft_dice
# en: The Dice Under the Bridge
title [35192f] = 桥下的骰子
# en: {&Under the middle bridge the old cellars ring with dice. River water drips through the vaults; nobody looks up. At the long table a croupier with a rake calls the throws, and a seat is open, for anyone with coin and nerve.|The Undercroft's long table is quiet tonight, a few serious players and a croupier who rakes you a seat without a word. The drip from the vault lands, steadily, on the croupier's hat.|The dice table is three deep tonight; a ship's in, and its crew are losing their wages with great cheer. The croupier finds you a seat anyway.}
text [87c254] = {&中桥底下的老地窖里骰子声不绝。河水从拱顶滴下来，没人抬头看。长桌边一个拿着耙子的庄家报着点数，空着一个座位，给任何有钱有胆的人。|地下赌窟的长桌今晚很安静，几个认真的玩家，庄家一言不发地用耙子给你拨出一个座位。拱顶的水滴不停地落在庄家的帽子上。|今晚骰子桌边围了三层人；有条船进了港，船员们正兴高采烈地输掉工钱。庄家还是给你找了个座位。}
# en: A vaulted brick cellar lit by lanterns, river water dripping from the arches, a crowd around a long dice table, a croupier with a rake, a student with a stake in hand.
scene [14d7ad] = 灯笼照亮的砖砌拱顶地窖，河水从拱顶滴落，一群人围着长长的骰子桌，一个拿着耙子的庄家，一个学生手里拿着赌注。
# en: Play the dice
opt.left.label [5ff89b] = 掷骰子
# en: {&You read the table, the croupier's rake, the man who's sure he's lucky. You win twice, and quit while it's true. The croupier nods at you as if you'd done something rude.|You win, and the croupier, dripped on again, rakes your winnings over with a sigh. You tip him, which he didn't expect.|You win the sailors' wages off them, and then, because they're so cheerful about it, buy their supper. You still come out ahead.}
opt.left.say.1 [73aff4] = {&你看透了这张桌子、庄家的耙子，还有那个笃定自己走运的人。你赢了两把，趁好就收。庄家冲你点点头，好像你做了什么失礼的事。|你赢了，又被滴了一下的庄家叹着气把赢的钱耙给你。你给了他小费，他没想到。|你把水手们的工钱赢了过来，然后因为他们输得太开心，请他们吃了晚饭。你还是赚了。}
# en: {&You lose your stake in three throws, all of them close. The croupier rakes it away without looking, like a man brushing crumbs.|You lose, and the croupier's hat, dripped on again, seems to cheer up.|The sailors win everything tonight, including your stake. They're very sorry about it, and buy you a drink.}
opt.left.say.2 [fffc87] = {&三把就输光了赌注，每把都只差一点。庄家看都不看就把钱耙走了，像在扫面包屑。|你输了，又被滴了一下的庄家的帽子似乎高兴了起来。|今晚水手们赢走了一切，包括你的赌注。他们很过意不去，请你喝了一杯。}
# en: Mind the door for the house
opt.right.label [7d7392] = 替赌场看门
# en: {&The house pays a coin a night for a pair of eyes on the iron door. You stand in the drip with the doorman, saying the word to people who know it and "No" to people who don't. A fence buys a ship's clock off a sailor right in front of you. You take the coin, and feel dirtier for it.|You mind the door. A man in a magistrate's coat comes in with his collar up and nods to you, as if you'd agreed never to have seen him. You're paid; you're cold.|A watchman comes down the steps, takes his envelope from the doorman, and goes out again without looking at the tables. You get paid too. It's an education, and a cold one.}
opt.right.say.1 [1c8fa6] = {&赌场每晚出一枚硬币，雇一双眼睛盯着那扇铁门。你和看门人一起站在滴水里，对知道暗语的人说出暗语，对不知道的人说“不行”。一个销赃人就在你眼前以十分之一的价钱从一个水手手里买下一座船钟。你收下硬币，觉得自己脏了。|你看门。一个穿治安法官外套的人竖着领子进来，冲你点点头，好像你们说好了你从没见过他。你拿了钱；你很冷。|一个巡警走下台阶，从看门人手里接过他的信封，看都没看赌桌一眼就出去了。你也拿到了钱。这是一堂课，一堂冷冰冰的课。}

@event undercroft_pit
# en: Fight Night
title [dc2f33] = 擂台之夜
# en: It's fight night in the Undercroft. In the sawdust pit a dock giant with fists like mallets is facing a small, quiet woman who keeps her hands low. The bookmaker is offering long odds on the woman, which means he knows something, or wants you to think he does.
text [fcc766] = 今晚是地下赌窟的擂台之夜。铺着锯末的坑里，一个拳头像木槌的码头巨汉对上一个双手垂得很低、安静的小个子女人。庄家给那个女人开出很高的赔率，这说明他知道点什么，或者想让你以为他知道。
# en: A sawdust fighting pit in a brick cellar under a bridge, two bare-knuckle prize-fighters circling, a roaring crowd waving betting slips, a bookmaker taking a student's coin.
scene [a66673] = 桥下砖砌地窖里铺着锯末的擂台坑，两个赤手空拳的拳手在绕圈，咆哮的人群挥着赌票，一个庄家正收下一个学生的硬币。
# en: Bet on the small woman
opt.left.label [a9199f] = 押那个小个子女人
# en: She lets the giant swing himself tired for two rounds, then puts him in the sawdust with one short punch. The cellar goes silent, then mad. The bookmaker pays you with a face like a wet week.
opt.left.say.1 [76d0d9] = 她让巨汉挥拳挥了两个回合挥到脱力，然后一记短拳把他打倒在锯末里。地窖先是一片死寂，然后沸腾了。庄家付钱时脸拉得像连阴天。
# en: The giant catches her in the second round and that's that. She's up again before they count her out, and bows to him. You've lost your stake. You find you don't mind as much as you should.
opt.left.say.2 [6fb4db] = 第二回合巨汉逮住了她，就此结束。她在读秒结束前站了起来，向他鞠了一躬。你的赌注输了。你发现自己并没有该有的那么在意。
# en: Go and see the fighters after
opt.right.label [9b0c5a] = 散场后去见见拳手
# en: You go round the back after the bout. The small woman, it turns out, was a sailor, and a duellist's bodyguard, and is now a fishwife on weekdays. She shows you how to stand, and pushes you over to prove you're standing wrong. Your shoulder aches for a day.
opt.right.say.1 [f60c9c] = 散场后你绕到后面。原来那个小个子女人当过水手，当过一位决斗者的保镖，现在平日里是个卖鱼妇。她教你怎么站，又把你推倒来证明你站错了。你的肩膀疼了一天。

@event undercroft_fence
# en: No Questions
title [5f8c67] = 不问来历
# en: In an alcove off the dice hall sits the Undercroft's fence, a soft-spoken man in a velvet waistcoat with a table of watches, rings and candlesticks that all used to belong to someone. He looks you over through his loupe. "Academy," he says. "I could use a pair of young eyes. Somebody to tell me which of these are enchanted. Paid, of course. No questions."
text [60cc09] = 赌厅旁的一个凹室里坐着地下赌窟的销赃人，一个穿天鹅绒背心、说话轻声细语的男人，桌上摆着怀表、戒指和烛台，每一件都曾属于某个人。他透过放大镜打量你。“学院的，”他说，“我正缺一双年轻的眼睛。告诉我这里头哪些是附了魔的。当然有报酬。不问来历。”
# en: A dim cellar alcove under a bridge, a soft-spoken fence in a velvet waistcoat behind a table of watches, rings and silver, holding a jeweller's loupe, looking at a student.
scene [984642] = 桥下昏暗的地窖凹室，一个穿天鹅绒背心、说话轻柔的销赃人坐在摆满怀表、戒指和银器的桌子后，手持珠宝放大镜看着一个学生。
# en: Appraise his stock for him
opt.left.label [d1be8b] = 替他鉴定货物
# en: You go through his table with a fingertip and a word, sorting the enchanted from the merely stolen: a ring that warms, a watch that runs backwards, a candlestick that remembers its family. He pays well, and politely, and you can't stop thinking about the family.
opt.left.say.1 [35f39f] = 你用一根指尖和一句咒语把他的桌子过了一遍，把附了魔的和单纯偷来的分开：一枚会发热的戒指，一块倒着走的表，一个记得自己主人家的烛台。他付得很大方，也很客气，而你一直忘不掉那户人家。
# en: Turn him down
opt.right.label [b56858] = 拒绝他
# en: "No," you say. He smiles, unoffended, and goes back to his loupe. "Everybody says no once," he says. You walk out past the dice knowing he'll be in that alcove, with that loupe, whenever you change your mind.
opt.right.say.1 [a50c06] = “不，”你说。他笑了笑，并不介意，又低头看他的放大镜。“人人都会拒绝一次，”他说。你穿过骰子桌走出去，知道只要你改了主意，他就会在那个凹室里，拿着那只放大镜。

@event rookery_rooftops
# en: The Roofs of Port Calder
title [3521ca] = 考尔德港的屋顶
# en: {&Up on the Rookery the city is a different place: chimney-pots and washing lines, gutters for roads, and below, the whole capital lighting itself for the night, from the cathedral's spire to the masts in the harbour.|The way up to the Rookery is the water-butt, the outhouse roof and the drainpipe that holds if you don't trust it too long. At the top, washing lines and a cat who owns the street.|On the Rookery tonight there's mist on the sea and the lamps of the bridges are coming on one by one, upriver. Somebody's chalked a star on the nearest chimney.}
text [908e69] = {&在鸦巢上，城市是另一副模样：烟囱帽和晾衣绳，檐沟当路，下方整座王都正为夜晚点起灯火，从大教堂的尖塔一直到港里的桅杆。|上鸦巢的路是雨水桶、茅房顶，还有那根只要你别太信它就撑得住的落水管。顶上是晾衣绳，还有一只统治整条街的猫。|今晚鸦巢上，海面起了雾，上游几座桥的灯一盏接一盏亮起。有人在最近的烟囱上用粉笔画了一颗星。}
# en: The crowded rooftops of an old harbour town at dusk, chimney-pots and washing lines, a student sitting on a roof ridge looking out over a lamp-lit city and the sea.
scene [75610e] = 黄昏时一座老港镇拥挤的屋顶，烟囱帽和晾衣绳，一个学生坐在屋脊上眺望灯火通明的城市和大海。
# en: Run the old routes
opt.left.label [06326a] = 跑一趟老路线
# en: {&You run the routes across three streets without touching the ground: gutter, ridge, a jump over an alley that's wider than it looks. You land laughing on the last roof, and a cat applauds.|You run the long way, past the cat, and take the long jump at the dyers' yard. The washing on the lines flaps at you like a crowd.|You run the Rookery end to end and back again in the mist, by memory, and never slip once.}
opt.left.say.1 [045454] = {&你沿着路线跑过三条街，脚不沾地：檐沟，屋脊，跳过一条比看上去更宽的小巷。你笑着落在最后一个屋顶上，一只猫为你鼓掌。|你绕远路，经过那只猫，在染坊院子那儿完成了长跳。晾衣绳上的衣服像观众一样冲你拍打。|你在雾里凭记忆把鸦巢从头跑到尾再跑回来，一次也没滑倒。}
# en: {&A slate slides under your boot and you go down the roof on your back into a gutter full of leaves. Bruised, filthy, alive.|You misjudge the dyers' yard and land in the washing. The washing comes down with you. A dyer shouts things.|You slip in the mist and catch a chimney-pot, and the chimney-pot holds, just. You climb down very slowly.}
opt.left.say.2 [d1dc37] = {&一块瓦片在靴底下滑走，你仰面顺着屋顶滑进一条满是落叶的檐沟。一身瘀青，一身脏，还活着。|你在染坊院子那儿判断失误，掉进了晾晒的衣服里。衣服跟着你一起掉了下去。一个染工骂骂咧咧。|你在雾里一滑，抓住了一个烟囱帽，烟囱帽勉强撑住了。你非常慢地爬了下来。}
# en: Sit on the ridge and watch the city
opt.right.label [5ab614] = 坐在屋脊上看城市
# en: {&You sit on the ridge with your knees up and watch the capital light itself, street by street, until it's all lamps. You'll never see it like this from the ground. The slates are cold, and you stay far too long.|You sit and watch the ships come in under lamps, and the castle feels a long way off. Up here it's all just lights, and a wind off the sea that gets into your bones.|You sit in the mist with the bridges coming on upriver, for a long time. You climb down damp through, sneezing.}
opt.right.say.1 [fec96a] = {&你抱着膝盖坐在屋脊上，看着王都一条街一条街地亮起来，直到满城灯火。在地面上你永远看不到这样的景象。石板瓦冰凉，你待得太久了。|你坐着看船在灯火下进港，城堡显得很远。在这上面，一切都只是灯光，还有一阵从海上吹来、钻进骨头里的风。|你坐在雾里，上游的桥一座座亮起，坐了很久很久。爬下来时你浑身湿透，喷嚏不断。}

@event rookery_old_marks
# en: Chalk on the Chimneys
title [424666] = 烟囱上的粉笔记号
# en: {has(origin_street): On a chimney by the old crossing, still there under the soot, are the chalk marks your crew left when you were small, a star for a safe roof, a cross for a loose slate, and your own mark, the one you made up at nine. Somebody has gone over them since, to keep them fresh.|On a chimney by an old crossing are chalk marks, layers of them, years deep, stars and crosses and arrows and a little drawn eye. The crews' code. Someone keeps them fresh.}
text [10e006] = {has(origin_street): 老路口旁的一根烟囱上，煤灰底下仍留着你小时候伙伴们画的粉笔记号，星是安全的屋顶，叉是松动的瓦片，还有你自己的记号，是你九岁时编的。有人后来又描过，让它们保持清晰。|一个老路口旁的烟囱上有粉笔记号，一层叠一层，积了好些年，星、叉、箭头，还有一只小小的眼睛。是街头帮伙的暗号。有人一直在把它们描新。}
# en: A rooftop at night, faded chalk symbols on a brick chimney, a student tracing them with a finger, the lit city below.
scene [4db3be] = 夜晚的屋顶，砖砌烟囱上褪色的粉笔符号，一个学生用手指描摹着，下方是灯火通明的城市。
# en: Check the roof the marks promise
opt.left.label [4568ae] = 检查记号担保的那片屋顶
# en: {has(origin_street): One of the stars, fresh, says the roof past the chimney is sound. You know that roof, and test it, and it isn't: two slates go under your boot. You rub the star out and chalk a cross. Somebody from the loft will be glad, and never know why. Your shin is scraped.|One star says the roof beyond is sound. You test it, carefully, and a slate slides out under your boot into the street. You rub out the star and draw the only mark you're sure of, a cross. Your shin is scraped.}
opt.left.say.1 [1cae5f] = {has(origin_street): 有一颗新画的星说烟囱那边的屋顶是结实的。你认得那片屋顶，一试，并不结实：两块瓦片在你靴下碎了。你擦掉那颗星，画了个叉。阁楼里的某个人会因此庆幸，却永远不知道为什么。你的小腿擦破了。|一颗星说那边的屋顶是结实的。你小心地试了试，一块瓦片从你靴下滑出去，掉到了街上。你擦掉那颗星，画上你唯一确定的记号：一个叉。你的小腿擦破了。}
# en: Learn to read them
opt.right.label [bdf544] = 学着读懂它们
# en: {has(origin_street): You sit by the chimney and read the marks again, slowly, the way you used to. Some are new. One says a roof you loved has gone loose. One says the watch has a new man on the quay. You feel nine years old and far from home.|You sit for an hour working the marks out against the roofs around you: stars where the slates are sound, crosses where they aren't. By the end you can read a little of the crews' code. It feels like eavesdropping.}
opt.right.say.1 [626ff1] = {has(origin_street): 你坐在烟囱边，像从前那样慢慢地重读这些记号。有些是新的。一个说你喜欢的某片屋顶松了。一个说码头上来了个新巡警。你觉得自己又成了九岁，离家很远。|你坐了一个小时，对照周围的屋顶琢磨这些记号：星代表瓦片结实，叉代表不结实。到最后你能读懂一点街头帮伙的暗号了。感觉像在偷听。}

@event rookery_watch_guide
# en: The Watch Wants a Guide
title [6338eb] = 巡警要个向导
# en: Lanterns on the ladder at the end of the street: the watch is coming up onto the Rookery, which it hardly ever does. Somebody robbed a house on the Crescent tonight. The sergeant heaves himself onto the roof, sees you, and holds out a coin. "You know these roofs," he says. "Show us the ways across. The crews' ways."
text [1d202d] = 街尽头的梯子上亮起了灯笼：巡警要上鸦巢来了，这种事几乎从没有过。今晚新月街有户人家被盗。警长费力地爬上屋顶，看见了你，递过来一枚硬币。“你熟悉这些屋顶，”他说，“带我们走过去的路。街头帮伙走的路。”
# en: A rooftop at night, a burly watch sergeant with a lantern hauling himself onto the roofs from a ladder, holding out a coin to a student by a chimney, the lit city below.
scene [bfa86e] = 夜晚的屋顶，一个提着灯笼的魁梧巡警警长正从梯子爬上屋顶，向烟囱边的一个学生递出一枚硬币，下方是灯火通明的城市。
# en: Lead them the long way round
opt.left.label [777179] = 带他们绕远路
# en: You lead the watch along every gutter but the right ones, with great earnestness, for an hour, until the sergeant is stuck astride a ridge and swearing. Somewhere far off, a skylight closes. The sergeant never works out what you did. He thanks you.
opt.left.say.1 [1cf9e4] = 你一脸诚恳地领着巡警走遍了所有不对的檐沟，走了一个小时，直到警长骑在一道屋脊上下不来，骂个不停。远处，一扇天窗关上了。警长始终没弄明白你干了什么。他还谢了你。
# en: The sergeant is no fool. Two roofs in he stops, looks at the chalk on a chimney, looks at you, and sends you down the ladder with a long stare. By morning Port Calder knows the academy student wouldn't help the watch, and the watch knows it too.
opt.left.say.2 [942fe4] = 警长可不傻。走过两个屋顶，他停下来，看看烟囱上的粉笔记号，又看看你，用长长的一眼把你打发下了梯子。到早上，考尔德港都知道那个学院学生不肯帮巡警，巡警也知道。
# en: Show them the crews' ways
opt.right.label [c02770] = 带他们走帮伙的路
# en: You show them: the dyers' yard jump, the sailmaker's skylight, the chimney with the star. They catch nobody tonight, but now they know. The sergeant pays you. Every chalk mark you pass on the way down looks at you.
opt.right.say.1 [ece60b] = 你带他们走了一遍：染坊院子的跳跃，制帆铺的天窗，画着星的烟囱。今晚他们谁也没抓到，但现在他们知道了。警长付了你钱。下来的路上，你经过的每一个粉笔记号都在看着你。
